/* Cut under the both-sports rule: he wants to run cross country <em>and</em> track, and a
   program that sponsors one without the other cannot give him both. Every school here does
   sponsor men’s cross country — several were measured on it, one at target tier — which is why
   they were on the board at all. Each was checked twice: the school’s own athletics site sport
   list and published track roster — several list a “track and field” page whose roster is entirely
   women — and then TFRRS for the school’s men at their conference indoor and outdoor
   championships, where a sponsored program must appear. Individual men from a cross country
   roster do post open-meet marks without a men’s track program existing, so a single TFRRS mark
   is not the test; absence from every conference championship is. The cross country numbers are
   kept intact below because they are true and because the rule, not the running, is what removed
   these schools. See methodology.html §6b. */
